Long output from the bash tool now keeps its end. Before, once output passed 256 KB, every later line was dropped, so the model never saw the test result: or error summary of a long cargo test or build. Now it gets the first half, the newest half, and between them ... (output truncated: N bytes omitted) ..., which is the same wording yoagent 0.27.5 uses in its own bash. Committed as f7116cae, titled "Part of #1159" because item 2 is the next task.

• New `src/bash_output_cap.rs`: a HeadTailCap accumulator. It never cuts inside a multi-byte character, and any bytes skipped to avoid that are counted in N, so kept plus omitted always equals the total; a test checks this. Output under the cap is byte-identical to the input. Seven unit tests cover under-cap input, the first and last lines surviving, the exact count, the marker text, multi-byte characters at many cap sizes, and many small pushes giving the same result as one big push.
• `src/tools.rs`: StreamingBashTool uses the new accumulator. The final result, the timeout's "Output so far" and the live updates all show the same head-and-tail text. I removed a truncated flag that was written but never read, so the file went from 5295 to 5286 lines, and I updated its entry in tests/module_size.rs.
• Tests updated, none deleted:
  • The old truncation test only checked "says truncated or is short". It now checks the first line, the last line, the marker, and that the middle is gone.
  • The timeout test used to assert that the tail was dropped, which pinned the old bug. It now asserts the tail is kept and the middle is dropped.
• Positive control: blanking the tail in the output turned 6 tests red, both tool-level ones included. I restored it in the same command and everything was green again.
• Docs: no user page describes the bash cap, so only ARCHITECTURE.md changed. Its new entry says this is a hand copy of a private yoagent struct and marker. It can drift, and the marker test only pins the literal string, not yoagent's live behaviour.

